{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Gerrit 1983 patchset 2 — addressed an LLM-Review -1 (tests only)\n\n**Finding (valid):** `fit_preserving_marker`'s undecorated fast path\n(`outbound_comments.py:256`, `if not text.endswith(RECONCILER_MARKER): return fit(text)`)\nwas untested, even though the change explicitly contracted it as \"descriptions and\nundecorated bodies stay byte-identical\". A guarantee asserted in prose and not pinned.\nThat branch carries every non-comment caller, so its blast radius is wider than the\nmarker path that WAS tested.\n\n**Fix:** `fit_preserving_marker` is now driven directly against the real `AdfCodec`\nfitter over 8 shapes — empty, short, multiline, a marker-lookalike ending in `-->`,\ntrailing-newline and trailing-space bodies, and two OVER-limit bodies — each asserting\nbyte-identity with a bare `fit(text)`. A companion test proves the over-limit case\ngenuinely truncates, so the two sides are not trivially agreeing by returning the input.\n\n**Mutation check — the first version had no teeth, and the check caught it.** The\nsuggested mutation (`rstrip()` on the fast path) initially SURVIVED: none of my inputs\nhad trailing whitespace left after fitting (the over-limit ones end in the truncation\nnotice, the rest in prose), so `rstrip` was a no-op on every case. That is precisely the\ntautology a mutation check exists to expose. The `trailing_whitespace` and\n`trailing_spaces` cases were added to close it. Three mutations now all return RED:\n\n| mutation | result |\n|---|---|\n| A — fast path `.rstrip()` | 2 failed |\n| B — fast path decorates undecorated text | 9 failed |\n| C — fast path removed entirely | 3 failed |\n\n**Gates on patchset 2:** ruff clean; complexity ratchet `active=49 new=0 increased=0\nstale=0`; mypy `613 source files` clean; full unit suite **11951 passed, 44 skipped, 0\nfailed**. No production code changed from patchset 1 — tests only. Amended onto the same\n`Change-Id` (`I2d6d36f…`), so this is patchset 2, not a duplicate change. No `recheck`\nwas issued: `Verified` was already +1, so this was a review finding, not a CI fault."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787300996037728001,"uuid":"8a021f8d-9a6a-4385-be32-bcdb62197ab5"}